Andy,
I, too, am running RH7.1 on a 600au... Works well for the most part but
there have been some issues along the way.

1.  Netscape works until I make any changes to the preferences.  When I
go into preferences to set up mail or internet proxies, it works until I
close it but hangs when I restart it.  Removing the preferences.js file
lets it start working again, but then I can't set up anything in the
preferences.

2.  I had to manually run sndconfig to get the sound running. I think I
chose soundblaster 16 and I guessed at the values until it started
working.

3.  I had trouble with RHN as well, but I thought it was just because I
had to set up http/ftp proxies to get through our firewall.  Downloading
the latest versions of the rhn and up2date rpms fixed it - I think there
are 2 or 3 of them.

4.  I have trouble with Xcdroast - cdda2wave seems to lock up the whole
system if I tell Xcdroast to read from a cdrom.  I have to make sure my
cdrom and cdrw trays are both empty before I start it up, then I can
only burn files/iso's that I have already saved to disk - can't copy
cds.  I think I just need to update/recompile the sources but I haven't
taken the time.

I only use KDE, so I'm a bit inexperienced with the Gnome stuff.  If you
want to use KDE, DEFINATELY download KDE2.2.1 - it's way better.
Although now I have to login via the console and then type startx - but
again, that's because I haven't taken the time to fix it.

Good Luck...
Terry

