> Now i'm confused this service says i had a connection of 288kbps whilst
> netscape told me it was downloading the
> kernel at 60kbps. This is a 512kbps connection with two pc's attached
> which may explain the 288kbps figure.

2wire may be giving you an *optimum* connection thier test site while
linuxiso may be slower if it's busy. the 288 reflects the speed of 2wire
to you. linuxiso to you may vary. the test is what your line is capable
of if servers feed it at optimum speeds.

i get quite slow speeds sometimes when a server is busy. my 2wire test
speeds are usually between 800 and 1000kbps. earlier this morning i
upgraded my ximian desktop and only got speeds of 10 kbps at times. i am
sure it was because ximian was busy.

i have 4 computers attached to the same connection and it does not
reflect a change in bandwidth unless others are pulling down data.

