I have a very odd problem.  I am using my Multia as my firewall /
router.  It is a great little box that I have had for years.  It has
unfortunatly become unreliable over the years but I've been helping it
(clipping thermocouple, heatsinking the ship on the bottom)...

My one annoyance is that the onboard interface eventualy (about 10 days
uptime) stops being able to dhcp to the cable company.  I *think* its a
media detection problem.  I did however try each and every driver (using
2.2.18 tulip,old_tulip,de4x5)...  There were some media warnings that got
me looking at this.  Weird thing is that the pci 10/100 adapter I use is
also dec chip and has worked flawlessly on the internal network.  I have
never seen this problem
before -- even with the same kernel.  I move the cable modem closer adn to
a more reliable cable, still no dice.  Has anyone else seen this?

the *only* way I have found to fix this problem is a restart (though a
soft (back to milo) will do it)...  removing modules and reinstalling /
changing mods will not do it.

hints tips?  sugestions?

