On Sun, 14 Oct 2001, tony.icuc wrote:
> I have been running MySQL on Alpha with RH 7.1 wonderfully stable for 45 
> days.  I was wondering if anyone knew of an ODBC driver/service for Alpha 
> Linux such that I could query the DB from a Windows workstation using MS 
> Office.

I think this is what MyODBC is for.  You shouldn't need to install
anything on your alpha-linux box; myODBC runs on Windows and speaks the
native MySQL wire protocol.

It's been about two years since I tried this myself... I had some trouble
with Access, but MS Query worked fine.  The ODBC driver is much improved,
judging by the release notes:

ftp://sunsite.dk/mirrors/mysql/Downloads/MyODBC/ReleaseNotes

Jeff




