Hi,

The ram that was in my LX164 is, for the moment, in an Asus P3B-F, and the BIOS screen that
I see when I boot the Asus motherboard always shows the memory as having SPD, no matter
what I set it to(SPD, or User-defined, or 125MHz(8 ns)) in the BIOS.
That's why I'm wondering if SPD memory can be used in an LX164.
The memory is Mitsubishi MH8S72ALD-10 676C011E 64MB 9x(8Mx8) ECC, unbufferred.
I cannot find anything on the web about whether it has an SPD EEPROM or not. 
Should I be able to tell if the memory module has an EEPROM chip on it by looking at it?

Most x86 motherboards that call for PC100 memory will work with PC133 memory
