With regards to your message at 05:50 AM 10/23/01, Nikolaos A. Margaritis. 
Where you stated:
>-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----
>Hash: SHA1
>
>Isn't there something we could do about the alpha RH issue?
>A web petition or something?
>- --
>Dr. Nikolaos A. Margaritis

It is easy to "do something" about it:

All we have to do is make sure that we can guarantee Red Hat that they will 
sell "XXX" copies of boxed product, and I am certain they would support this.

They ARE a business, and they are supposed to try and make some money!

If you are unhappy, don't blame Red Hat.
Blame Compaq.

While you are at it, if you have Compaq equipment, I suggest that you 
should call them up and demand they refund your money, as they devalued the 
Alpha machines you bought with their poorly thought out strategy and 
announcements.

A lot of you made purchasing decisions based on statements by Compaq 
regarding the "future of Alpha" and Compaqs commitment to it.

If so, they lied to you. I suggest you demand your money back.

But please, do not blame Red Hat. They had nothing to do with it.


